# Card UI Composition

When editing or creating card UIs, always follow the app design system and keep information hierarchy clear.

## Required structure for data cards

1. Primary title on its own line (`card-subtitle`), never merged with secondary metadata.
2. Secondary metadata (ex.: aluno) on a separate line with subdued style (`text-sm text-light`).
3. Status badge aligned in the header opposite the title (same row, no overlap/wrap collisions).
4. Date/info block below header (`protocol-meta` or equivalent), one item per line.
5. Actions in a dedicated footer row (`btn-group`) with existing semantic button classes.

## Data fallback rules

- Never show misleading placeholders when data exists in alternate contract fields.
- For person labels, prefer composed full name from `firstName` + `lastName`, then fallback to email.
- For date labels, never render `Invalid Date`; show a safe fallback (`-`) for missing/invalid values.

## Do / Don't

```jsx
// ✅ Good: clear hierarchy
<h3 className="card-subtitle">{protocol.name}</h3>
<div className="text-sm text-light">Aluno: {studentLabel}</div>

// ❌ Bad: mixed lines and broken hierarchy
<h3 className="card-subtitle">{protocol.name} Aluno: {studentLabel}</h3>
```
